 "_comment": [
  "The simulated internet for every lab. Every address comes from a documentation range",
  "(RFC 5737 IPv4, RFC 3849 IPv6) and every ASN from the documentation ranges (RFC 5398: 64496-64511",
  "and 65536-65551), so nothing here can ever point at a real network. demo_site/lab_edge.py accepts",
  "X-Lab-Client-IP only for addresses inside these pools; tools/labclient.py picks source addresses from them.",
  "`type` is ground truth for the scoreboard and is NEVER exposed to defenses: they must infer",
  "it from data/feeds/* (built by tools/build_world.py), like a production stack would.",
  "Allocation: 192.0.2.0/24 residential ISPs; 198.51.100.0/24 mobile, corporate, universities,",
  "privacy relays (.0-.95), then cloud_gcp (.96/27), free_proxy (.128/26), bulletproof_host (.192/27);",
  "203.0.113.0/24 datacenter, hosting, VPN, Tor, open proxies (full); 2001:db8::/32 one /48 or /64 per",
  "pool that needs a large fleet (2001:db8:10x::/48 for the spread residential-proxy pools).",
  "Optional pool keys (tools/build_world.py): `spread` (one host per /N, e.g. 64), `listed` (share of a",
  "per-address feed that lists the pool), `feeds` ({feed: true|false} overrides the type's defaults).",
  "`groups` names a set of pools a client can rotate over as one (tools/labclient.py world_pool).",
  "See workshops/STORE_CONTRACT.md before adding a pool."
 ],
